              "text": "To log in to Microsoft OneDrive, you can use any of the options below depending on how you want to access your files:\n\n### 1. Log in via Web Browser (Easiest)\n1. Go directly to the **[OneDrive Sign-in Page](https://onedrive.live.com)**.\n2. Click **Sign in** if you aren't redirected automatically.\n3. Enter the **email address, phone number, or Skype name** associated with your Microsoft account (personal, work, or school) and click **Next**.\n4. Enter your **password** and click **Sign in**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Log in on Your Computer (Windows or Mac)\nIf you want your files to sync directly to your computer's folders:\n* **On Windows:** Press the `Windows Key`, type **OneDrive**, and open the app. (If you use Windows 10 or 11, it is already pre-installed).\n* **On Mac:** Open **Finder**, go to **Applications**, and open **OneDrive** (you can download it from the Mac App Store if you don't have it).\n* **Sign in:** Once the setup window opens, enter your Microsoft account email and password to begin syncing your files.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Log in on Mobile (iPhone, iPad, or Android)\n1. Download the free **Microsoft OneDrive** app from the Apple App Store or Google Play Store.\n2. Open the app and enter your Microsoft account credentials to log in.",
